\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Design of the study. The 445 individuals with both expression and phase 3 genotypes are drawn one dot per person, European above the axis and Yoruba below. Filled European dots are the 87 individuals in random draw 1; the same draw was repeated five times. The stems are the real elastic-net weights for DNAJB7, a gene examined in detail later, with the European model above and the Yoruba model below. Every pair of models feeds the variance decomposition and the summary-statistic TWAS.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:design}{{1}{5}{Design of the study. The 445 individuals with both expression and phase 3 genotypes are drawn one dot per person, European above the axis and Yoruba below. Filled European dots are the 87 individuals in random draw 1; the same draw was repeated five times. The stems are the real elastic-net weights for DNAJB7, a gene examined in detail later, with the European model above and the Yoruba model below. Every pair of models feeds the variance decomposition and the summary-statistic TWAS}{figure.1}{}}
