\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces How much the answer depends on the draw. The decomposition is run twice against the same Yoruba sample, using two independent random draws of 87 European individuals. (a) Each gene's weights share in one draw against the other. (b) Which component is largest for a gene, one draw against the other. (c) The median share of each component, one dot per draw.}}{13}{figure.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:replicates}{{12}{13}{How much the answer depends on the draw. The decomposition is run twice against the same Yoruba sample, using two independent random draws of 87 European individuals. (a) Each gene's weights share in one draw against the other. (b) Which component is largest for a gene, one draw against the other. (c) The median share of each component, one dot per draw}{figure.12}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces What each population can see of the other's models. The SNVs selected by usable models, binned by their minor allele frequency in the other population, European models above the axis and Yoruba models below. The leftmost bin holds variants that are rare or absent there.}}{13}{figure.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:coverage}{{13}{13}{What each population can see of the other's models. The SNVs selected by usable models, binned by their minor allele frequency in the other population, European models above the axis and Yoruba models below. The leftmost bin holds variants that are rare or absent there}{figure.13}{}}
